course: dictionary
lesson: 2668
title: Words about health
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about how the body works, and diabetic is one of them. A diabetic is a person who has diabetes, an illness where the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood properly. The sentence «It is not caused by eating sweets and you cannot catch it» tells you that diabetes is not something you can catch from another person.
explain: Diabetic can also describe things connected with diabetes. Look at the word next to it: «diabetic food», «diabetic care», «diabetic nurse». In each phrase, diabetic tells you what kind of food, care or nurse it is.
explain: Context helps you see which job a word is doing. Ask yourself: is the word describing a thing, or naming a person? That quick check tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Diabetic means having diabetes.
fact: A diabetic is a person who has diabetes.
fact: Diabetes is an illness where the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood properly.
fact: The body uses a hormone called insulin to control blood sugar.
fact: «A diabetic child can even eat the birthday cake» when careful carb counting is part of their care.
exercise: «It is not caused by eating sweets and you cannot catch it.» What does this sentence tell you about diabetes? | *It is not caused by sweets and cannot be caught from another person | It is caused by eating too many sweets | You can catch it from a friend
exercise: A school nurse says, «Our diabetic nurse helps children check their blood sugar.» What does diabetic mean here? | Made of sugar | *Connected with diabetes | Very fast
exercise: Mia says, «A diabetic is a kind of sugary food.» Is Mia right? | No, a diabetic is a sort of cake | *No, a diabetic is a person who has diabetes | Yes, a diabetic is a sweet
test: Which hormone does the body use to control blood sugar? | Adrenaline | Keratin | *Insulin
test: Your diabetic friend feels shaky and faint. What should you do? | Ignore it and keep playing | *Tell an adult straight away, as they may need sugar quickly | Run away and hide
exam: Which sentence uses diabetic as a noun, meaning a person? | Diabetic friendly cake is on the shelf | The diabetic care at the clinic was kind | *Maya is a diabetic and checks her blood sugar every day | Diabetic food is labelled on the box
